From b3f2850d05580c3aa83b73a696ea0d1e67b47120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:03:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 68/68] macro_rules: accept the `expr_2021` fragment specifier

Rust 1.83 added `expr_2021`, the `expr` fragment as it was before the
2024 edition extended it with `const { .. }` blocks and `_`. Crates on
edition 2024 that keep a macro's old behaviour use it. ar_archive_writer
0.5.3 (src/coff_import_file.rs, via jql 9.0.3):

    macro_rules! u16 {
        ($val:expr_2021) => { object::U16::new(object::LittleEndian, $val) };
    }

    coff_import_file.rs:35-40 error:0: Unknown fragment type 'expr_2021'

mrustc's `expr` matcher has neither extension, so `expr_2021` maps to
the same pattern kind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/macro_rules/parse.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp b/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp
index acd109bf..5552c220 100644
--- a/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp
+++ b/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp
@@ -152,6 +152,8 @@ public:
                     ty = MacroPatEnt::PAT_PATH;
                 else if( type == "expr" )
                     ty = MacroPatEnt::PAT_EXPR;
+                else if( type == "expr_2021" )  // 1.83: `expr` without the 2024-edition additions (`const {}`, `_`) - the same here
+                    ty = MacroPatEnt::PAT_EXPR;
                 else if( type == "stmt" )
                     ty = MacroPatEnt::PAT_STMT;
                 else if( type == "ty" )
